# CommentsService — Change log

[English](change.log) · [Русский](change.log.ru) · [Українська](change.log.ua)

## 1.1.0.2 VisualStudio — 2026-10-29

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.2_VisualStudio`

- Added CommentsService.slnx for opening the existing API and React files in Visual Studio 2026.
- Frontend files are solution items; building the solution builds the API. Docker still builds the complete application.
- Updated all three READMEs and read.me; kept version 1.1.0.2 and the planned next iteration unchanged.
- Validation: .NET CLI lists the API project; Release solution build in Ubuntu passed with zero warnings/errors. Opening the solution in Visual Studio itself was not verified.

## 1.1.0.2 Docker — 2026-10-29

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.2_Docker`

- Added multi-stage Docker builds for React/.NET and one same-origin application container.
- Added PostgreSQL development storage and an optional persistent test database with separate volumes and credentials.
- Bootstrap creates non-superuser application roles only on empty volumes; ordinary restarts do not recreate databases.
- Added application/container readiness checks, static frontend serving and correct 404 responses for unknown API routes.
- Added one-time private environment generation that preserves existing files; credentials and local files are excluded from Git/build context.
- Added the rule that extra work uses the same version with a different branch description, without shifting planned iterations.
- Updated all three README languages, read.me and the development plan. No EF models/migrations or comment features yet; configuration version remains 0.
- Validation: Docker Release/frontend build and all three container health checks passed.
- Verified both databases retain probe records and the same volumes after container recreation; cleaned up only owned probes afterwards.
- Verified database role restrictions, non-root app execution, credential-file preservation and no private files in the image.
- Edge checks passed: same-origin API/frontend, version 1.1.0.2, health, API 404, SPA fallback, 360 px layout and no JavaScript errors.

## 1.1.0.1 Init — 2026-10-29

Branch: `CommentsService/v_1.1.0.1_Init`

- Started a new independent development history at Init.
- Added a minimal .NET 10 API with GET /api/status.
- Added an English React start page showing the backend connection state.
- Added build/run instructions, versioning rules and the agreed incremental plan.
- Documentation update within Init: README.md is English, README.RU.md is Russian,
  README.UA.md is Ukrainian; removed the redundant README.en.md and updated language links.
- All supporting documentation is maintained in English, Russian and Ukrainian.
- No database, migrations, comment features, Docker deployment or configuration extraction yet.
- Validation: .NET Release build passed with zero warnings/errors; TypeScript/Vite
  production build passed. Edge verified API metadata, connected/unavailable states,
  English UI, no comments form/API, no JavaScript errors and no overflow at 360 px.
- No unit/integration suite is included in Init; database tests belong to later steps.
- Split the change log into change.log (English), change.log.ru (Russian) and change.log.ua (Ukrainian).
